1
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:23,290
A Real Stewart

2
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:26,660
There's nothing more joyous than the arrival of a new baby.

3
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,630
I am so excited. Mother!

4
00:00:28,630 --> 00:00:31,860
Just imagine--Marilyn and Richard must be thrilled!

5
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:34,020
Oh, a new baby!

6
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:38,710
Max ... Max ... Max.

7
00:00:38,710 --> 00:00:44,050
Oh, it's a sweet-sounding name for a sweet little boy.

8
00:00:44,050 --> 00:00:47,160
My first grandchild.

9
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:50,150
And my first nephew.

10
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:52,860
Isn't he just adorable?

11
00:00:52,860 --> 00:00:55,640
He looks a lot like you, Mom. He does.

12
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:59,090
Do you think so?

13
00:00:59,090 --> 00:01:02,010
Well, I guess. He does look a lot like Richard,

14
00:01:02,010 --> 00:01:05,870
and I guess he looks a lot like me.

15
00:01:05,870 --> 00:01:08,970
Oh, he's got Richard's eyes, though.

16
00:01:08,970 --> 00:01:13,040
I really want Harry and Michelle to see Max.

17
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:14,070
When are they coming?

18
00:01:14,070 --> 00:01:17,650
Tomorrow. Harry has an account to work on today.

19
00:01:17,650 --> 00:01:22,040
Yes, he does have Richard's eyes. Big blue eyes.

20
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:24,270
[01:20.17]The baby even looks at you like Richard does.

21
00:01:24,270 --> 00:01:26,940
Well, children usually resemble their parents.

22
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:28,550
It's true.

23
00:01:28,550 --> 00:01:31,590
Michelle is a lot like Harry in so many ways.

24
00:01:31,590 --> 00:01:36,200
And she's shy with new people, just like he is.

25
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:39,140
You really like Michelle, don't you?

26
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:41,890
Yes. I'm very fond of her.

27
00:01:41,890 --> 00:01:46,360
And Harry, too?

28
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:47,400
Well ...

29
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:50,310
Uh, it's four-thirty. Oh my!

30
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:52,760
Marilyn and Richard will be home from the hospital any minute,

31
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:55,410
and we must prepare this room.

32
00:01:55,410 --> 00:01:58,230
Where will we put all the presents?

33
00:01:58,230 --> 00:02:01,110
Well, let's take everything to the living room.

34
00:02:01,110 --> 00:02:04,470
Marilyn and Richard and the baby need the space.

35
00:02:04,470 --> 00:02:08,050
It's crowded in here.

36
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:09,980
The welcome sign is up:

37
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:11,660
"Welcome home, Max."

38
00:02:11,660 --> 00:02:14,210
Isn't it exciting, Grandpa?

39
00:02:14,210 --> 00:02:17,190
Your first great-grandchild.

40
00:02:17,190 --> 00:02:21,040
Yes. Yes, sir.

41
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:25,400
A great-grandchild. A great-grandson.

42
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:28,940
Another generation to carry on the Stewart name.

43
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:30,550
I love you, Grandpa.

44
00:02:30,550 --> 00:02:35,060
You make me feel so proud to be part of our family.

45
00:02:35,060 --> 00:02:37,500
One day, you'll have your own family,

46
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:40,950
and I'll be proud to be part of it.

47
00:02:40,950 --> 00:02:43,940
Now you understand my feelings, Susan.

48
00:02:43,940 --> 00:02:48,210
I'm Grandpa's daughter-in-law, but I feel like a Stewart.

49
00:02:48,210 --> 00:02:51,230
He's always made me feel like his own daughter.

50
00:02:51,230 --> 00:02:52,140
Well,

51
00:02:52,140 --> 00:02:58,880
that's because you're so much like us--wonderful!

52
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:04,950
Mom, got it.

53
00:03:04,950 --> 00:03:07,690
This will make a nice gift for Marilyn and Richard.

54
00:03:07,690 --> 00:03:09,930
They can keep a record of all of the important dates

55
00:03:09,930 --> 00:03:12,760
and information about Max's life here.

56
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:14,630
Let's see.

57
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:18,090
Name: Max Stewart.

58
00:03:18,090 --> 00:03:20,030
Does he have a middle name?

59
00:03:20,030 --> 00:03:24,130
No, just Max. I like that.

60
00:03:24,130 --> 00:03:26,650
No middle name. No middle initial.

61
00:03:26,650 --> 00:03:30,430
Like me. I'm Malcolm Stewart.

62
00:03:30,430 --> 00:03:33,130
Just Malcolm Stewart.

63
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:35,100
And Max has your initials, Grandpa:

64
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:42,630
Uh, it must mean something.

65
00:03:42,630 --> 00:03:46,090
Weight: eight pounds six ounces.

66
00:03:46,090 --> 00:03:49,810
Eight-six. Big boy!

67
00:03:49,810 --> 00:03:51,980
All the Stewart men were big.

68
00:03:51,980 --> 00:03:54,980
Well, Robbie was eight pounds two ounces,

69
00:03:54,980 --> 00:03:57,670
and Richard was eight pounds three.

70
00:03:57,670 --> 00:03:59,840
And me?

71
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:02,510
Eight pounds six.

72
00:04:02,510 --> 00:04:06,020
You were big, just like Max.

73
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:08,230
Eight pounds six, just like me.

74
00:04:08,230 --> 00:04:11,680
That's nice. Length. Length?

75
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:15,530
Richard says Max is twenty-one inches long.

76
00:04:15,530 --> 00:04:18,450
Twenty-one inches.

77
00:04:18,450 --> 00:04:21,210
Is that tall or average or what?

78
00:04:21,210 --> 00:04:25,940
Tall. All the Stewart men are tall.

79
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:31,770
Well, Grandpa, you're about five-nine or five-ten.

80
00:04:31,770 --> 00:04:35,280
I wouldn't call that tall.

81
00:04:35,280 --> 00:04:37,380
I take after my mother's family.

82
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:43,070
They were ... they were ... they were average.

83
00:04:43,070 --> 00:04:50,820
Mother: Marilyn. Father: Richard.

84
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:56,170
And lots of pages for Richard's photos of Max.

85
00:04:56,170 --> 00:04:59,370
Speaking of mother and of father

86
00:04:59,370 --> 00:05:02,620
--and speaking of Max--I hear the car.

87
00:05:02,620 --> 00:05:03,700
They're here!

88
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:08,870
Oh! Oh, quickly! Go, go, go!

89
00:05:08,870 --> 00:05:12,230
Let's see. Oh, welcome home.

90
00:05:12,230 --> 00:05:13,050
Oh, let her in.

91
00:05:13,050 --> 00:05:14,430
Wait with your pictures for a second.

92
00:05:14,430 --> 00:05:17,030
Come on, darlings.

93
00:05:17,030 --> 00:05:21,720
Sweetheart .... Sit down right here.

94
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:26,610
Oh, he's so cute! Oh, Marilyn!

95
00:05:26,610 --> 00:05:28,970
Max looks just like Grandpa.

96
00:05:28,970 --> 00:05:30,870
A real Stewart.

97
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:33,870
I'm so happy to be home with my family--and with Max.
